"title": "Yahweh (YHWH)",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "yahweh yhwh",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<h1>YAHWEH (YHWH)</h1><p>Yahweh is the personal name of God in the Old Testament. In Hebrew it is written with four consonants, transliterated YHWH. It is usually translated “LORD” in English Bibles.</p><p><em>See</em> <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"4667\" data-resource-code=\"AquiferOpenBibleDictionary\">Names of God</data>.</p>",
