{
"content_id": "9102",
"reference_id": 8270,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Year",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "year",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<h1>YEAR</h1><p>A year is a period of twelve months. In the Bible, a year usually consisted of twelve lunar months. In some years, an extra month was added to keep the calendar in line with the seasons.</p><p><em>See</em> <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"3559\" data-resource-code=\"AquiferOpenBibleDictionary\">Calendars (Ancient and Modern)</data>.</p>",
