{
"content_id": "9104",
"reference_id": 8272,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Yellow",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "yellow",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<h1>YELLOW</h1><p>A color that appears as golden, or like the sun or ripe lemons. In the Bible&apos;s laws about skin diseases, priests looked for yellow (or blonde) hair as a sign of infection (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"03013030\" data-end-ref=\"03013030\">Leviticus 13:30</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"03013032\" data-end-ref=\"03013032\">32</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"03013036\" data-end-ref=\"03013036\">36</data>). </p><p><em>See also</em> <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"3781\" data-resource-code=\"AquiferOpenBibleDictionary\">Color</data>.</p>",
